# Summary

- Verifies that synchronization creates a source memory document and registers it in indexes when no prior document exists.
- Verifies that unknown exported symbols are rejected before the memory store is modified.
- Verifies that an existing companion document is reported as updated and is re-written and re-indexed.
- Verifies JSON responses are rendered by the server with a source hash and without code fences.
- Verifies a single corrective generation when the initial structured response is invalid.
- Verifies rejection of code blocks and undeclared dependencies.
- Verifies ignored top-level model metadata and rejection of unknown nested JSON fields.
- Verifies model-provided gap objects are discarded before decoding.
- Verifies acceptance of valid JSON despite a mislabeled Markdown fence.
- Verifies selection of the final JSON response after a thinking block.
- Verifies repository-relative provenance rendering.
- Verifies selection of an LLM structured-generation capability when available.
- Verifies deterministic completion of an exported symbol omitted by the model.
- Verifies deterministic completion of an omitted summary and dependencies.
- Verifies rejection of unsupported line evidence and rendering of a test scenario only when it cites a parsed assertion.

# Coverage

- Covers creation result metadata, deterministic rendering, source-line provenance, semantic validation, repair, persistence and index calls, and validation-failure safety.
